## API Design Standards

- **Versioning**: Prefix all API routes with `/api/v1/` (or current version).
- **REST conventions**: Resource names use plural nouns, not verbs.
- **Consistent responses**: Use Laravel API Resources for all responses.

```
GET    /api/v1/positions          # List (paginated)
GET    /api/v1/positions/{id}     # Show
POST   /api/v1/positions          # Create
PUT    /api/v1/positions/{id}     # Full update
PATCH  /api/v1/positions/{id}     # Partial update
DELETE /api/v1/positions/{id}     # Delete
```

| HTTP Code | When to use |
|---|---|
| 200 | Success (GET, PUT, PATCH) |
| 201 | Resource created (POST) |
| 204 | Success, no content (DELETE) |
| 400 | Bad request |
| 401 | Unauthenticated |
| 403 | Forbidden (authenticated but unauthorised) |
| 404 | Resource not found |
| 422 | Validation failed |
| 500 | Server error |

